Description: AirPods management daemon and TUI for Linux
 Keyboard-driven TUI plus headless daemon speaking Apple's AACP control
 channel over Bluetooth L2CAP. Exposes per-pod battery, noise control modes
 (Off/Transparency/Adaptive/ANC), Conversation Awareness, One-Bud ANC,
 ear-detection pause/resume, stem media controls, volume swipe synced to
 system volume, and iPhone <-> Linux audio handoff. Includes a systemd user
 unit running the headless daemon (`systemctl --user enable --now
 airpods-tui`) and Waybar JSON output modes (`--waybar`, `--waybar-watch`).
 .
 NOTE: Apple AACP features require BlueZ to identify as an Apple device:
 `DeviceID = bluetooth:004C:0000:0000` under [General] in
 /etc/bluetooth/main.conf (not applied automatically by this package),
 followed by `sudo systemctl restart bluetooth`.
